Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:56:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 465/488] [DS4.1] Vision: B12X's SIMT projection for few rows,
 blocked K sums, reference GELU

Run 21's vision accuracy failures:
- At up to eight rows B12X projects through its SIMT GEMV (FP32 FMA chains,
  then warp and block butterflies), whose results are correctly rounded at
  one row; gemv_kernel reproduces it step for step, with the same bias,
  GELU and SwiGLU epilogues.
- The GEMMs sum each 64-wide K block from zero and add the blocks in FP32
  (the tensor core's accumulation no longer compounds over the whole K).
- GELU is DeepSeek's reference, torch's F.gelu (FP32 erff); B12X uses
  CuTe's erf, whose last bits differ (21 of 327680 aligner outputs): the
  difference is measured and bounded to one BF16 step.
